Subject: JRI / bug in RFactor with NAs
In-Reply-To: <229A0489-5934-4EA8-B2F6-8BBCA4517658@broad.mit.edu>
References: <FFD6D773-C5D2-4271-9DB5-43BC69E03B72@broad.mit.edu> <229A0489-5934-4EA8-B2F6-8BBCA4517658@broad.mit.edu>
Message-ID: <478C7843.1050503@gmx.net>

Dear Simon Urbanek,

there is another bug in RFactor (JRI), if you generate it with NAs.

Minimal example:

        String[] arg = {"--vanilla"};
        Rengine re = new Rengine(arg, false, null);
        String s = "as.factor(c(1,2, NA))";
        REXP exp1 = re.eval(s);
        RFactor f1 = exp1.asFactor();
        // ids get messed up : {levels=("1","2"),ids=(0,1,2147483647)}
        f1.at(2);
        // expectedly throws ArrayIndexOutOfBoundsException
        re.end();

Unfortunately the bug seems to be in the C code of Rengine.eval, so I 
was too lazy at the moment to track it there...

I have also tested the same code with Rserve, as I need it work there 
too, without any problems.

Regards,

Bernd Bischl

